6. Start A.D.A. during normal use
Once the Python project is configured and its launch command is confirmed, the routine will look like this:
# Start the local AI model
ollama run qwen3:1.7b


Then, in a second terminal, activate the Python environment and launch the A.D.A. application using its verified entry point.
Important: Running the model in Ollama proves that the language model works; it does not automatically start your custom A.D.A. interface, speech recognition, or dashboard.
For the exact final launch command, paste the output of these two commands from inside the extracted project directory:
find . -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort | head -200


find . -maxdepth 3 -type f \( -name "README*" -o -name "requirements.txt" -o -name "pyproject.toml" \)


